kai-ld: Heads-up: we need a final approach for fetch in the JS SDK. Edge-first customers keep pulling node polyfills into edge bundles. Options: require undici, optionalDep, or runtime-detect + docs.

anu-p: runtime-detect + docs. absolutely no implicit polyfills for edge builds. smaller bundles matter.

drew-sre: Agreed. Also we must support both ESM and CJS consumers. CJS users expect sync require side-effects sometimes, so provide a sync getter that returns null if no global fetch and an async loader for Node.

sam-eng: prototype I used in a PoC:

```js
// runtime-fetch.js (ESM-first)
export function getFetchSync() {
  return typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function' ? globalThis.fetch : null;
}

export async function loadFetch() {
  const f = getFetchSync();
  if (f) return f;
  const m = await import('undici');
  return m.fetch;
}
```

kai-ld: love it. couple of notes: - do NOT list undici in deps; documenting `npm i undici` for Node <20 is clearer. - add a debug log that prints which fetch we picked (helpful in support tickets).

anu-p: typings: TS consumers hit errors when our d.ts references RequestInit/Response from DOM. I propose shipping a tiny types file `types/fetch-lite.d.ts` that exports `type FetchLike = (input: any, init?: any) => Promise<any>`. Re-export it from the main types. That avoids forcing \"lib\": [\"DOM\"].

drew-sre: runtime differences: Bun/Node/Workers handle streaming differently. Add a normalizeBody util that accepts string/Buffer/ReadableStream/AsyncIterator/ArrayBuffer and normalizes to Node Buffer or ReadableStream depending on target runtime. Tests should cover those shapes.

kai-ld: packaging nuance: pnpm hoisting can still pull optional deps into installs. Docs should include pnpm/webpack/next.config tips to ensure undici isn't accidentally bundled into an edge build.

anu-p: on retries/auth: implement retries and token-refresh at SDK layer (above fetch). That keeps behavior consistent regardless of fetch impl. Expose low-level agent options only when undici present.

sam-eng: CI matrix proposal: Node 16/18/20 (with and without undici), Bun, Deno (compat), Cloudflare Workers (miniflare). Also a smoke test that asserts debug log contains \"fetch=global\" or \"fetch=undici\".

doc-bot: reminder: create ticket DX-512 for TS types and DX-513 for CI matrix.

kai-ld: docs checklist: 1) README section \"Which fetch will the SDK use?\" 2) Next.js examples (edge vs server) 3) TS FAQ + copy/paste fixes 4) pnpm/webpack FAQ 5) Debugging tips (how to enable SDK debug logs).

anu-p: small ergonomic API idea: export `getFetchSync()` and `initFetch()` where initFetch returns a Promise and logs the chosen implementation. That keeps require() consumers able to check at startup and ESM users can await.

drew-sre: tests should assert normalizeBody works across runtimes and that retries trigger token-refresh hook when 401 returned.

sam-eng: action items: - implement runtime-fetch utilities + CJS shim (sam) - add types/fetch-lite.d.ts and export FetchLike (anu) - docs + Next.js/Vite/webpack examples (kai) - CI matrix + tests (drew)

kai-ld: decision: runtime-detect + no undici in package.json, ship fetch-lite types, provide clear docs and debug logs. I'll mark this as chosen and expect PRs.

sam-eng: will open PR with code + tests + docs later today and ping reviewers. thanks!
